      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ALSOBROOK: No, sir. We -- we're saying that under 1441 that because the district court retained jurisdiction, that that was original jurisdiction to remove the matter, and that actually, Your Honor, when we removed this, they -- the majority of circuit courts of appeals, namely the second, sixth, seventh, and eighth, had said that the proper vehicle to remove this was the All Writs Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "159f5b6059be291ddf161c298809f74d909c11efdcb0fdfac13ebc045fb6db59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-159f5b6059be-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But you have no right to remove under 1441 because there wasn't complete diversity in the Louisiana suit. Isn't that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Alsobrook",
      "case_id": "2002-01-757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "159f5b6059be291ddf161c298809f74d909c11efdcb0fdfac13ebc045fb6db59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-159f5b6059be-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And also because the majority of the circuits have approved the procedures that we followed in this case. You have the Second Circuit; you have the Sixth, Seventh, and Eighth."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Alsobrook",
      "case_id": "2002-01-757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "159f5b6059be291ddf161c298809f74d909c11efdcb0fdfac13ebc045fb6db59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-159f5b6059be-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The majority of the circuits have approved the procedures that we followed in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Bederman",
      "case_id": "2002-01-757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "159f5b6059be291ddf161c298809f74d909c11efdcb0fdfac13ebc045fb6db59",
      "evidence_id": "ev-159f5b6059be-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The All Writs Act may not be relied upon to remove an otherwise unremovable case. It is Congress's province to define the limits of removal, and chief of these is the requirement of original jurisdiction in Federal court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-757",
      "confidence": 1.0,
